module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.LinearGroupSchemes
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Grp
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Smooth
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.ClosedImmersion
public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsAlgClosed.AlgebraicClosure

/-! # A unitriangular embedding over the ground field

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Corollary 14.12, p.283, Theorem 14.5(a)-(b),
pp.281-282, and Corollary 3.35, p.75.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-geometric-unipotence-unitriangular-embedding).

The conclusion specifies the unitriangular subgroup by its polynomial coordinate chart:
the strict upper entries are the coordinate variables, the diagonal is one and the lower
entries are zero. The inclusion is a group homomorphism, so the law is matrix multiplication.
All schemes, charts and factorizations are over the original field.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory
open scoped MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A faithful representation with unipotent geometric points has a closed unitriangular
embedding over k, including a closed immersion into the unitriangular group itself.
The coordinate chart identifies that group with Spec k[x_ab : a < b]; under its inclusion
into GL_n a point corresponding to phi has entries phi(x_ab), 1, and 0 above, on, and below
the diagonal respectively. The test algebras include nonreduced algebras and the zero ring.

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Corollary 14.12, p.283, Theorem 14.5(a)-(b),
pp.281-282, and Corollary 3.35, p.75.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-geometric-unipotence-unitriangular-embedding).

Proof plan:
1. By lem-sfb-geometric-unipotence-faithful-closed-immersion the given rho is a closed
   immersion: GL_m is affine of finite type by def-sc-general-linear-group and injectivity
   holds on all algebra-valued points, not only field-valued points.
2. Inductively construct a flag F_r of k-subspaces in k^m. In a basis extending F_r,
   the lower-right block gives the rational quotient action on W = k^m/F_r. Nilpotence
   of rho(g)-1 descends to this quotient for every geometric point.
3. When W is nonzero, apply lem-sfb-unipotent-matrix-group-fixed-vector to the image of
   G(K) in GL(W_K). Then lem-sfb-geometric-unipotence-invariant-descent supplies a nonzero
   vector of W fixed scheme-theoretically over k. Lift it to the next basis vector.
4. The kernel of R tensor k^m -> R tensor W is R tensor F_r, as is seen in the chosen
   basis. Thus the lifted vector extends the flag, and induction reaches a full basis.
   In this basis all R-valued matrices are upper unitriangular for every k-algebra R.
5. Conjugating rho by this k-basis preserves closed immersion. In the coordinates of
   GL_m the ideal generated by x_aa-1 and x_ab for b<a has quotient k[x_ab : a<b], since
   the determinant becomes one. Products and inverses preserve these equations; the
   inverse of 1+T is the finite sum of (-T)^s, since T^m=0. They define the group U below,
   its chart e and its closed inclusion j. Evaluate at the universal point of G to see
   that the coordinate map kills the ideal. Its induced map from the quotient is still
   surjective, so def-weil-closed-immersion gives the closed factor f. Take n=m. -/
theorem geometric_unipotence_unitriangular_embedding
    {k : Type u} [Field k] (G : Over (Spec (.of k))) [GrpObj G]
    [IsAffine G.left] [Smooth G.hom] [LocallyOfFiniteType G.hom] [QuasiCompact G.hom]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 0 < m)
    (rho : G ⟶ GeneralLinearGroup (ULift.{u} (Fin m)) k) [IsMonHom rho]
    (hinj : ∀ (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [Algebra k R],
      Function.Injective (fun x : (Spec (.of R)).asOver (Spec (.of k)) ⟶ G ↦ x ≫ rho))
    (hunip : ∀ x : (Spec (.of (AlgebraicClosure k))).asOver (Spec (.of k)) ⟶ G,
      ∃ N : ℕ, 0 < N ∧
        ((GeneralLinearGroup.homMulEquiv (ULift.{u} (Fin m)) k (AlgebraicClosure k)
          (x ≫ rho)).val - 1) ^ N = 0) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, 0 < n ∧ ∃ (U : Grp (Over (Spec (.of k))))
      (f : G ⟶ U.X) (j : U.X ⟶ GeneralLinearGroup (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) k),
      IsMonHom f ∧ IsMonHom j ∧ IsClosedImmersion f.left ∧ IsClosedImmersion j.left ∧
      IsClosedImmersion (f ≫ j).left ∧
      ∃ e : U.X ≅ (Spec (.of (MvPolynomial {p : Fin n × Fin n // p.1 < p.2} k))).asOver
          (Spec (.of k)),
        ∀ (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [Algebra k R]
          (phi : MvPolynomial {p : Fin n × Fin n // p.1 < p.2} k →ₐ[k] R) (a b : Fin n),
          (GeneralLinearGroup.homMulEquiv (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) k R
            ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom phi.toRingHom)).asOver (Spec (.of k)) ≫
              e.inv ≫ j)).val (ULift.up a) (ULift.up b) =
            if h : a < b then phi (MvPolynomial.X ⟨(a, b), h⟩)
            else if a = b then 1 else 0 := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
